==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|grc|δενδρίτης||of or pertaining to a tree}}. Equivalent to {{confix|en|dendr-|-ite}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈdɛndɹaɪt/|a=UK}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|cytology}} A slender projection of a [[nerve cell]] which conducts [[nerve impulse]]s from a [[synapse]] to the body of the cell; a [[dendron]].
#* '''1970''', {{w|Saul Bellow}}, ''{{w|Mr. Sammler's Planet|Mr. Sammler’s Planet}}'', Greenwich, CT: Fawcett, 1971, Chapter&nbsp;1, pp.&nbsp;12–13 ([https://archive.org/details/mrsammlersplanet1970bell online edition])
#*: Little copses of television antennas. Whiplike, graceful thrilling metal '''dendrites''' drawing images from the air, bringing brotherhood, communion to immured apartment people.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1979|author=w:Carl Sagan|chapter=Can We Know the Universe? Reflections on a Grain of Salt|editor=John Carey|title=Eyewitness to Science|publisher=Harvard University Press|year_published=1997|page=437
|passage=A typical brain neuron has perhaps a thousand little wires, called '''dendrites''', which connect it with its fellows.}}
# {{lb|en|cytology}} Slender cell process emanating from the cell bodies of dendritic cells and follicular dendritic cells of the immune system.
# {{lb|en|crystallography|metallurgy}} Tree-like structure of crystals growing as material crystallizes
# A [[hermit]] who lived in a [[tree]]

